// Draft — REQUIRES LEGAL REVIEW before DNS cutover.
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
---

<LegalPage
  title="Cookie Policy"
  heading="Cookie Policy"
  description="The cookies and similar technologies used on resultsmatrix.com, and how to control them."
>
  <p>
    This policy explains the cookies and similar storage that resultsmatrix.com (the "Site") uses.
    It should be read with our <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>. We use as little as we can:
    no advertising cookies, no remarketing, and no social media tracking pixels.
  </p>

  <h2>What these technologies are</h2>
  <p>
    Cookies are small text files a website stores in your browser. "Local storage" is a similar
    browser feature that keeps a small piece of data on your device. Both let a site remember
    something between pages or visits.
  </p>

  <h2>What the Site uses</h2>

  <h3>Strictly necessary</h3>
  <p>These do not need your consent because the Site cannot respect your choices without them.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>rml-cookie-consent</strong> (local storage). Remembers whether you accepted or
      declined analytics cookies, so we do not ask you on every page. It stays until you clear
      your browser data or change your choice.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Form security check.</strong> Our forms use Cloudflare Turnstile to tell people from
      automated bots. It runs a short check in your browser and may process your IP address and
      browser signals to do so. We use it to protect the forms, not to track you.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Analytics (only if you accept)</h3>
  <p>
    If you press Accept on the banner, the Site loads HubSpot's tracking script, which sets the
    cookies below. They tell us which pages are visited, how long people stay, and how they
    arrived, and they let HubSpot link a later form submission to your earlier visits. If you
    decline, none of this loads.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>hubspotutk</strong>. Identifies you as a visitor. Typically lasts about 6 months.</li>
    <li><strong>__hstc</strong>. Records visit times and counts. Typically lasts about 6 months.</li>
    <li><strong>__hssc</strong>. Tracks the current session. Typically lasts 30 minutes.</li>
    <li><strong>__hssrc</strong>. Detects whether your browser restarted. Lasts for the session.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    HubSpot sets these on our behalf and describes them in
    <a href="https://knowledge.hubspot.com/privacy-and-consent/what-cookies-does-hubspot-set-in-a-visitor-s-browser" rel="noopener noreferrer">its cookie documentation</a>.
    Lifetimes can change on HubSpot's side.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <p>
    Use the button below to reopen the banner and change your choice at any time. If you switch
    from Accept to Decline, the tracking script stops loading on your next page, and you can also
    delete the cookies above in your browser settings. Most browsers also let you block or delete
    cookies altogether. Blocking local storage means the Site cannot remember your choice, so
    the banner may reappear.
  </p>
  <p>
    <button
      type="button"
      onclick="window.rmlResetConsent && window.rmlResetConsent()"
      class="cursor-pointer font-sans text-sm font-medium text-accent-700 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-accent-800"
    >
      Change your cookie choice
    </button>
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If we add or remove a cookie or tracking tool, we will update this page and the effective date
    above before it goes live, and ask for your consent again where the law requires it.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions: <strong><a href="mailto:info@resultsmatrix.com">info@resultsmatrix.com</a></strong>.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
